course: dictionary
lesson: 11204
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «A wolf spider mother carries her egg sac.» Here wolf is part of a name, and the word spider is the clue: this is a kind of spider, not a wild animal of the dog family.
explain: Wolf can also be a verb. In «Sam wolfed down his lunch», the word down is a clue. It means he ate very quickly in big mouthfuls. Ask yourself: is wolf doing something, or is it the name of a thing? That question shows you which meaning to use.
explain: Phrases change the meaning too. «The wolves howled to call the rest of the pack» uses wolf as a noun, a wild animal. But «Don't cry wolf» means raise a false alarm, which is not about animals at all. When a word sits next to other words in a set phrase, check whether the phrase has its own meaning.
fact: A wolf is a wild animal of the dog family that lives and hunts in groups called packs.
fact: As a verb, «wolf» or «wolf down» means to eat food very quickly in big mouthfuls.
fact: Wolves are rarely dangerous to people, but in fairy tales the wolf is often the clever, scary villain.
fact: «A lone wolf» is one wolf that acts alone, and «a pack of wolves» is a group of them.
fact: «Cry wolf» means raise a false alarm, and «a wolf in sheep's clothing» means someone who hides a bad nature behind a kind face.
exercise: «A wolf spider mother carries her egg sac.» In this sentence, what is a wolf? | *A kind of spider | A wild animal that lives in a pack | A pet dog | A greedy person
exercise: Dad says, «Stop wolfing your dinner!» What does wolfing mean? | Hunting in a pack | Cooking slowly | *Eating very quickly in big mouthfuls | Howling at the moon
exercise: «Don't cry wolf, or nobody will believe you.» What does cry wolf mean? | *Raise a false alarm | Pretend to be kind | Run very fast | Howl loudly to call the pack
test: Complete the phrase: «a ___ of wolves ran over the hill.» | Flock | Pride | Herd | *Pack
test: «He is a wolf in sheep's clothing.» What does this mean? | Someone who wears woolly jumpers | *Someone who hides a bad nature behind a kind face | A sheep that is hungry | A lone wolf that is lost
exam: In which sentence is wolf a verb? | The wolf howled at the moon | The wolf in the story was clever | A wolf lives in a pack | *Jamie wolfed down his toast
